              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                New Wheybolic's serving is two scoops and 50 g of protein, so a 26-serving tub holds 52 scoops. Some Amazon listings count one-scoop servings instead. Divide the price by total grams of protein and multiply by 25. That is the only fair way to compare it with brands that list one scoop as a serving.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Paying full price on Amazon</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                At the price we saw, the 26-serving tub on Amazon cost about $2.31 per 25 g of protein, more than Dymatize ISO100 and far more than Gold Standard. GNC's own price was lower, and its buy-one-get-one deals can halve it. Buy Wheybolic on a GNC promotion or buy a rival.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying old stock by mistake</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Original 40 g Wheybolic is still listed on Amazon at 20 g per scoop with Velositol. It is cheaper per gram there, but it is the old formula, without the Informed Choice claim on the new tubs. Check for New Wheybolic or Wheybolic Original on the label, and check the best-by date.
              </p>
