            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>What is the difference between old Wheybolic and New Wheybolic?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  The old formula gave about 20 g of protein per scoop, 40 g per two-scoop serving, with Velositol and a lactase and bromelain enzyme blend. The 2026 New Wheybolic gives 25 g per scoop and 50 g per serving, drops Velositol and the enzymes, keeps 6.2 g of leucine per serving, and adds Informed Choice and Informed Protein certification claims.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>How much protein is in one scoop of Wheybolic?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  New Wheybolic lists 25 g of protein and 3.1 g of leucine per scoop at the time of writing, in a scoop of about 32.4 g for Chocolate Fudge and 30.5 g for Classic Vanilla. The label serving is two scoops, 50 g of protein. The old formula gave about 20 g per scoop, so check which version you have.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is Wheybolic Informed Choice certified?</h3></summary>
